===Preposition===
{{en-head|prep}}

# Not [[position]]ed upon; away from a position upon.
#: {{ux|en|He's '''off''' the roof now.}}
#: {{ux|en|I took it '''off''' the table.}}
#: {{ux|en|Keep '''off''' the grass.}}
# [[detached|Detached]], [[separated]], [[excluded]] or [[disconnected]] from; away from a position of [[attachment]] or [[connection]] to.
#: {{ux|en|The phone is '''off''' the hook}}
#: {{ux|en|The coat fell '''off''' the peg.}}
#: {{ux|en|He was thrown '''off''' the team for cheating.}}
#: {{ux|en|We've been '''off''' the grid for three days now.}}
#: {{ux|en|We're '''off''' their radar.}}
#: {{ux|en|He's '''off''' the computer, but he's still on the phone.}}
# Outside the [[area]] or [[region]] of.
#: {{ux|en|The suspect is now believed to be '''off''' the campus.}}
#: {{ux|en|Water runs '''off''' the fields into the valley.}}
#: {{ux|en|Sweat was running '''off''' her forehead.}}
#: {{ux|en|I couldn't see what it said because the line of text ran '''off''' the page.}}
# Temporarily not [[attending]] (a usual place), especially owing to illness or holiday.
#: {{ux|en|'''off''' work; '''off''' school}}
# {{n-g|Used to indicate the [[location]] or [[direction]] of one thing relative to another, implying [[adjacency]] or [[accessibility]] via.}}
#: {{ux|en|His office is '''off''' this corridor on the right.}}
#: {{ux|en|We're just '''off''' the main road.}}
#: {{ux|en|Look! There's a UFO '''off''' our left wing!}}
## {{n-g|Used to express location at sea relative to land or mainland.}}
##: {{ux|en|The island is 23 miles '''off''' the cape.}}
## {{rfv-sense|en}} {{n-g|Used to indicate separation from a natural home or origin.}}
##: {{ux|en|He used to be gone a lot of the time, '''off''' working on an oil rig.}}
# Removed or subtracted from.
#: {{ux|en|There's 20% '''off''' the list price.}}
# No longer wanting or taking.
#: {{ux|en|He's been '''off''' his feed since Tuesday.}}
#: {{ux|en|He's '''off''' his meds again.}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial|more properly 'from'}} [[out of|Out of]] the possession of.
#: {{ux|en|He didn't buy it '''off''' him. He stole it '''off''' him.}}
# {{rfd-sense|en|section=off (2)}} {{non-gloss|Placed after a number (of products or parts, as if a unit), in commerce or [[engineering]]{{C|en|Engineering}}.}}
#: {{ux|en|I'd like to re-order those printer cartridges, let's say 5-'''off'''.}}
#* ''Tantalum bar 6 '''off''' 3/8" Dia × 12"'' — Atom, Great Britain Atomic Energy Authority, 1972
#* ''samples submitted … 12 '''off''' Thermistors type 1K3A531 …'' — BSI test report for shock and vibration testing, 2000
# {{lb|en|slang|[[drugs]]}} [[under the influence|Under the influence]] of.
#: {{ux|en|The guy was '''off''' a perc.}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} As a result of; resulting from the actions of.
#: {{ux|en|The team won '''off''' a late-game fumble by an opposing player.}}
#: {{ux|en|The economy is rising '''off''' the strength of the tech sector.}}
#: {{ux|en|Smith hit a home-run '''off''' the pitcher.}}

